{"chunk_id": "797b15a6caab", "text": "Vasishtha summons the brahmins, ministers, princes, and army chiefs to a grand assembly after King Dasaratha\u2019s death. The court fills with chariots, elephants, and nobles, and Bharata\u2019s arrival brightens the gathering as if the late king himself had returned. Presiding over the council, the sage Vasishtha urges Bharata to accept the throne, arguing that Dasaratha and Rama\u2019s obedience to duty have left the prosperous kingdom in his hands. Bharata, however, is deeply distressed. Invoking the ancient law that the eldest son must rule, he refuses to take Rama\u2019s rightful kingdom and condemns the injustice caused by his mother\u2019s actions. Declaring that both the throne and he himself belong to Rama, Bharata vows to go into the forest, bring Rama back, and if he fails, remain there with him.\nBharata rejects the throne offered by Vasishtha and vows to go to the forest to bring Rama back to rule Ayodhya.\nThemes: dharma and rightful kingship, loyalty to Rama, renunciation of power, moral integrity, assembly of sages and ministers", "vector": [0.008333015255630016, -0.02062707580626011, -0.026447385549545288, -0.005294866394251585, -0.0182423647493124, 0.02557164430618286, -0.027430910617113113, -0.001345610129646957, -0.01789206825196743, -0.004173243883997202, 0.01327084843069315, -0.014537304639816284, 0.0011519365943968296, 0.02426476962864399, -0.013445996679365635, 0.005837152246385813, 0.04742475599050522, -0.011546311900019646, 0.03721226751804352, -0.007578530348837376, 0.008346487767994404, -0.00841385219246149, 0.0030465691816061735, 0.027215342968702316, -0.02051929198205471, 0.0024638643953949213, 0.022715380415320396, -0.017703445628285408, 0.007538111414760351, -0.011963972821831703, -0.001899684895761311, -0.01981869898736477, -0.0024874419905245304, -0.013082226738333702, -0.030502742156386375, 0.008730466477572918, -0.011438528075814247, -0.012226695194840431, 0.025342604145407677, -0.00779409706